umpy can you guys please remove this ea launcher or whatever the f this is. i feel like my freedom is being taken away everytime it pops in the screen then will crash my game whenever it wants", "timestamp_created": 1677562505, "timestamp_updated": 1677562505, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 14, "votes_funny": 2, "weighted_vote_score": "0.670890927314758301", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "133777525", "author": {"steamid": "76561197994207456", "personaname": "yoshifreak", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197994207456/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 23, "playtime_forever": 5515, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5220, "last_played": 1677765147, "avatar": "3114ec61f2b07844841190a4e38e79003cd935c7"}, "language": "english", "review": "The combat and exploration is the best part of this game, and stands out compared to the original trilogy. And while the story does have interesting moments, especially where your companions are concerned, ultimately that's an important part that doesn't live up to the Mass Effect name. \nThere's definitely interesting ideas that get setup up but they payoffs are a bit hit or miss, and the long term consequences of player choices tend to be a bit unremarkable. \nOverall, it's still enjoyable but it's definitely a better action game than an RPG.", "timestamp_created": 1677552130, "timestamp_updated": 1677552130, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.511450350284576416", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887420", "reactions": []}]}